1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,668
A language needs recurring symbols, but fitted Gaussian parameters are not naturally unique.

2
00:00:05,668 --> 00:00:14,908
Two optimization runs can describe the same visual field with different row order, slightly shifted centers, and different rotation parameterizations.

3
00:00:14,908 --> 00:00:20,884
Quantizing raw parameter tuples would spend vocabulary capacity on accidental coordinate choices.

4
00:00:20,884 --> 00:00:23,533
The first job is therefore not compression.

5
00:00:23,533 --> 00:00:29,632
It is to define a stable physical alphabet whose tokens preserve rendering and spacetime structure.

6
00:00:30,332 --> 00:00:34,849
A unit quaternion q and its negation represent exactly the same rotation.

7
00:00:34,849 --> 00:00:44,191
Even after choosing quaternion sign, covariance eigenvectors may permute when their eigenvalues are reordered, and each eigenvector admits a sign flip.

8
00:00:44,191 --> 00:00:49,450
Feeding scale plus quaternion to a prior makes identical ellipsoids appear far apart.

9
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:56,318
This is pure representational noise: it changes parameter coordinates without changing a single rendered pixel.

10
00:00:57,018 --> 00:01:03,599
The canonical representation stores the matrix logarithm of the symmetric positive-definite covariance.

11
00:01:03,599 --> 00:01:07,368
A symmetric three-by-three matrix needs six unique numbers.

12
00:01:07,368 --> 00:01:13,693
The logarithm maps multiplicative scale differences into a well-behaved Euclidean coordinate chart.

13
00:01:13,693 --> 00:01:19,699
Decoding exponentiates, eigendecomposes, and converts one valid rotation back to the renderer.

14
00:01:19,699 --> 00:01:25,321
Any sign or axis choice made during that last factorization renders the same covariance.

15
00:01:26,021 --> 00:01:33,791
The first vocabulary treated an eight-Jewel constellation as one joint one-hundred-and-seventy-six-dimensional prototype.

16
00:01:33,791 --> 00:01:39,891
That couples layout, covariance, surface color, and color gradient into one indivisible choice.

17
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:42,074
Gate zero-a falsified that design.

18
00:01:42,074 --> 00:01:51,385
The successful language assigns independent codebooks to physical roles, then composes their aligned prototypes back into the same constellation.

19
00:01:51,385 --> 00:01:55,880
Factorization lets reusable geometry combine with reusable appearance.

20
00:01:56,580 --> 00:02:07,071
Four one-thousand-and-twenty-four-way decisions expose up to one-thousand-and-twenty-four to the fourth role combinations without fitting that impossibly large joint table.

21
00:02:07,071 --> 00:02:16,160
For individual generated Jewels, the centroid remains continuous and the three nonconstant roles—covariance, surface, and gradient—are active tokens.

22
00:02:16,160 --> 00:02:18,722
Layout becomes the spoken centroid itself.

23
00:02:18,722 --> 00:02:24,151
The codebooks share normalization and preserve the canonical twenty-two-feature contract.

24
00:02:24,851 --> 00:02:31,704
Cells are useful for learning local histograms and addressed phrases, but an address is not an emitted coordinate.

25
00:02:31,704 --> 00:02:35,492
The generator outputs centroids in continuous normalized space.

26
00:02:35,492 --> 00:02:40,782
Internal cell indices answer questions like which local token distribution applies here.

27
00:02:40,782 --> 00:02:43,427
They do not snap a Jewel to the cell center.

28
00:02:43,427 --> 00:02:50,881
This separation directly addresses the grid-quantization artifact: routing may be discrete while geometry remains irregular.

29
00:02:51,581 --> 00:03:09,235
At the selected individual-Jewel language gate, decoded irregular fields retain twenty-two-point-eight-six-five-seven decibels against the continuous source on the frozen random-volume audit, preserve mixed spacetime tilt at one-point-zero-four-one-five times the source, and show zero center locking.

30
00:03:09,235 --> 00:03:11,640
These numbers do not prove promptability.

31
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:20,203
They prove that the physical token vocabulary is not the bottleneck preventing a higher-level speaker from producing renderable continuous fields.
